$avatar — talking avatar video (SkyReels V3 A2V)

SUMMARY
  Generates a lip-synced talking-head MP4 from a portrait image and speech audio
  using the SkyReels V3 audio-to-video Comfy workflow (WanVideoWrapper, in-process
  via comfy_lib). Prototype: comfy_workflows/SkyReels-V3-Talking-Avatars.json.

SYNTAX
  $avatar
  $avatar(width=480, height=832, steps=4, fps=24)

INPUT
  images[]  — portrait / start frame (one per output, or one for all).
  sounds[]  — speech audio (.wav, .mp3, …); paired with images[].
  prompts[] — scene / motion prompt (what the avatar should do while speaking).
  negprompts[] — optional negative prompt links (else built-in default).

OUTPUT
  videos[] — MP4 with muxed input audio.
  images[] / sounds[] — cleared after run.

ARGUMENTS
  prompt= / neg= / negative_prompt= — override prompt text.
  width= / height= — output size (default: from input image, snapped to /16).
  steps= — diffusion steps (default 4, flowmatch_distill).
  seed= — base seed; offset per job when set.
  frames= / max_frames= — audio frame budget for MultiTalk (default 400).
  frame_window= — SkyReels window size (default 81).
  motion_frame= / drop_frames= — long-video overlap tuning (5 / 12).
  cfg= — classifier-free guidance (default 1).
  fps= — output frame rate (default 24).
  workflow= / json= — alternate API workflow JSON path.

DEPENDENCIES
  Same venv as $image2video: uv sync --extra media,comfy-wan,clip
  Models under models/ (diffusion_models, text_encoders, vae, transformers):
    Wan21-SkyReelsV3-A2V_fp8_scaled_mixed.safetensors
    Wan2_1_VAE_bf16.safetensors
    umt5-xxl-enc-bf16.safetensors

ENVIRONMENT
  AH_EMULATE_AVATAR=1 — write stub MP4 placeholders without loading models.
  AVATAR_WAN_MODEL / AVATAR_VAE / AVATAR_TEXT_ENCODER / AVATAR_WAV2VEC — overrides.
  AVATAR_ATTENTION_MODE — default sdpa; set sageattn if sageattention+triton installed.

EXAMPLE
  @face: $file('face.png')
  @voice: @text -> $text2speech(voice=af_bella)
  @clip: $avatar(width=480, height=832)
  A close-up portrait speaking naturally to camera
  @talk: @face -> @voice -> @clip

  Or pass prompt= on $avatar when the motion text must live on the wrapper @instruction.

PROMPT-CONSUMING
  Yes — prompts[] cleared on output.
